temperatures warm up in the valley one  woman is making sure infants and  children are comfortable in the water  with life-saving skills to prevent  drowning victoria saha joins us live in  henderson tonight with a look at how  crucial it is to start infant swimming  resource lessons victoria  a crystal clear pool like this can be so  tempting to jump into but small children  may not know how dangerous it could be  and in a blink of an eye they can find  themselves under water if no one is  paying attention  most parents think swim lessons are the  only way to teach your child how to be a  confident swimmer and stay above the  water but infant swimming resource also  known as isr is a crucial program that  teaches infants and young children how  to save themselves in the water by  breathing exercises and instant reflexes  like rolling onto your back instructor  jessica tuck says she starts teaching  infants as young as six months old  i have known people that have lost  kiddos to drownings amazing wonderful  parents who  love their kids and are attentive  parents and it still happens it happens  to good parents all the time  my boys did isr before i became an  instructor and i absolutely fell in love  with the program  safety doesn't just stop at the lessons  she says parents have to be very careful  and always make sure there are locked  gates surrounding a pool and if you're  having a gathering make sure there's  always a designated person to have an  eye on the children around the water  each lesson is about 10 minutes long  monday through friday for six weeks if  you are looking for an instructor make  sure they are certified we will have  more information up on our website at  8newsnow.com reporting live from  henderson tonight victoria saha live  local now
 

